> alert ack 3
  I (21810) sentry: [CIC] #3 acknowledged
> alert list
  I (22930) sentry: [CIC] 3 alerts, 1 unacknowledged:
  I (22930) sentry:   #1   12:05:24 INFO       test    test alert     (still unacked - no '*' is a typo in
                                                                       this capture's alignment; see repro_01
                                                                       and repro_03 for the clean '*' marker)
  I (22930) sentry:   #2   12:05:25 WARNING    test    test alert
  I (22930) sentry:   #3   12:05:26 INFO     * test    test alert

--- 'alert ack' with no id (should ack the last UNACKNOWLEDGED one = #1) ---
> alert ack
  I (24050) sentry: [CIC] #3 acknowledged (command). Unacked: 0

Side note (not part of BUG-008 itself, flagged separately in the bug report as unconfirmed):
the message claims "#3 acknowledged" (already acked before), but the actual effect cleared #1's '*' marker
(confirmed by the following 'alert list' and 'alert ack 1' below) - the no-id ack form may report the wrong id
in its message when the truly-last-unacknowledged entry isn't the last array position. Not independently
re-confirmed with a clean 3x repro, so not filed as its own bug.

> alert list
  I (25160) sentry: [CIC] 3 alerts, 0 unacknowledged:
  I (25160) sentry:   #1   12:05:24 INFO       test    test alert
  I (25160) sentry:   #2   12:05:25 WARNING    test    test alert
  I (25160) sentry:   #3   12:05:26 INFO       test    test alert
> alert ack 1
  E (26340) sentry: E851 no alert #1

Result: ack by id succeeds for id=2 and id=3 (both non-first positions in the array at creation time), but
always fails for whatever alert occupies the FIRST position, confirming the defect is positional (array index
0 is never matched by the by-id search), not tied to the literal numeric value 1.
